# Unencrypted source model - not used at runtime (only character.enc is
# loaded/decrypted client-side); kept locally for future edits, but must
# never be committed - it was LFS-tracked and broke Netlify's build (no
# LFS support), and publicly shipping it would defeat the point of
# encrypting character.enc in the first place.
